@distractor-lu Belsch

# --- Inanimate pronouns: m en, f/pl se, n et ---

@sentence
@lu D'Enveloppe ass kleng, mä se ass wichteg.
@en The envelope is small, but it is important.
@distractor-en parcel
@distractor-en heavy
@distractor-lu Pak
@distractor-lu schwéier

@sentence
@lu De Pak ass schwéier, mä en ass net ze grouss.
@en The parcel is heavy, but it is not too big.
@distractor-en letter
@distractor-en light
@distractor-lu Bréif
@distractor-lu liicht

@sentence
@lu D'Bréifboîte ass no bei der Post, mä se ass voll.
@en The letter box is near the post office, but it is full.
@distractor-en bank
@distractor-en empty
@distractor-lu Bank
@distractor-lu eidel

@sentence
@lu D'Päck sinn am Waardesall. Ech gesinn se.
@en The parcels are in the waiting room. I see them.
@distractor-en letters
@distractor-en stamps
@distractor-lu Bréiwer
@distractor-lu Timberen

# --- kee(n) / keng by gender and number ---

@sentence
@lu Ech hu keng Enveloppe bei mir.
@en I have no envelope with me.
@distractor-en parcel
@distractor-en stamp
@distractor-lu Pak
@distractor-lu Timber

@sentence
@lu Mir hu kee Pak fir Iech.
@en We have no parcel for you.
@distractor-en letter
@distractor-en stamp
@distractor-lu Bréif
@distractor-lu Timber

@sentence
@lu Mir hunn keng Timberen méi.
@en We have no stamps left.
@distractor-en parcels
@distractor-en envelopes
@distractor-lu Päck
@distractor-lu Enveloppen

@sentence
@lu Ech hu kee Bréif fir Iech.
@en I have no letter for you.
@distractor-en parcel
@distractor-en envelope
@distractor-lu Pak
@distractor-lu Enveloppe

@sentence
@lu Keng Suergen, ech fannen d'Post.
@en No worries, I will find the post office.
@distractor-en bank
@distractor-en letter
@distractor-lu Bank
@distractor-lu Bréif

# --- @fill: country and city prepositions -----------------------------------
# The country article stays inside the movement/position tile: a standalone
# `der` directly after `an` would violate the Eifeler-Regel blank constraint.

@fill
@lu Muer fueren ech [an d']Belsch.
@en Tomorrow I am travelling [to] Belgium.
@distractor-lu an der
@distractor-lu aus der
@distractor-lu op d'
@distractor-en in
@distractor-en from
@distractor-en near

@fill
@lu Haut sinn ech [an der] Belsch.
@en Today I am [in] Belgium.
@distractor-lu an d'
@distractor-lu aus der
@distractor-lu op der
@distractor-en to
@distractor-en from
@distractor-en near

